    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nIt feels good to use *mini.pick*!\n\n**Problem**\n\nHowever, there're cases where I'd like to move the caret to the front, and back.\n\nIt's hard for end users to define these actions.\n\n**Solution**\n\nDefine two actions `caret_home` and `caret_end`, and bind to `<Home>` and `<End>` by default.\n\nBrowsing the repo, it seems that `H.picker_move_caret` can already define these actions without friction.\n\nHopefully it will be implemented, thanks!",
