    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nUnfortunately, this is a bit problematic as there is no good default keys for these actions:\n\n- `<Home>` is by default used as [an alternative for `move_start`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-pick.html#minipick-actions-move), which I think is more useful as the default.\n- `<C-b>` (which is used in Command-line to move to its start) is used [for `scroll_up`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-pick.html#minipick-actions-scroll).\n\nAs on top of that I don't think these actions are frequently used (`delete_left` / `<C-u>` usually serves this purpose), it was decided to not add these actions. Especially, since they can mocked as custom \"repeat `<Left>` / `<Right>` many times\" mappings:\n\n```lua\nlocal make_home_end = function(direction)\n  return function()\n    local key = MiniPick.get_picker_opts().mappings['caret_' .. direction]\n    local n = #MiniPick.get_picker_query()\n    vim.api.nvim_input(string.rep(key, n))\n  end\nend\nrequire('mini.pick').setup({\n  mappings = {\n    caret_home = { char = '<Home>', func = make_home_end('left') },\n    caret_end = { char = '<End>', func = make_home_end('right') },\n  },\n})\n```",
            "created_at": "2026-05-26T13:43:37Z",
